<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Coalition Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Kokoomus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Coalition Party is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>'s main liberal-conservative party, founded in December 1918 by monarchist members of the old Finnish Party and Young Finnish Party. Long kept out of government during the Kekkonen era, it has since led several governments, and its members have included presidents <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sauli-niinisto">Sauli Niinistö</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-stubb">Alexander Stubb</a>. It supports a market economy and Finland's membership of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>.</p></div>
